    "formula_steps": [
      "Set x_0=0 at the 11:30 close and x_t=log(close_t/close_11_30) for each 13:01 through 15:00 bar end.",
      "For each t from 0 through 120 set peak_t=max(x_s for s<=t) and drawdown_t=peak_t-x_t.",
      "Let t_star be the earliest index attaining D=max(drawdown_t).",
      "Set R=x_120-x_t_star; by construction R is nonnegative because t_star attains the full-path maximum drawdown.",
      "Return R/(D+R)."
    ],
    "formula": "R / (D + R), where D is the maximum running-peak log drawdown on the 11:30 plus 13:01-15:00 close path, t_star is its earliest occurrence, and R is the terminal log-price recovery from x_t_star",
