    "hypothesis": "A high value indicates that after the strongest afternoon price shock, the stock recovered strongly into the close relative to the size of that shock; this close-known dip-absorption and liquidity-resilience state may persist from the next open through the third close.",
    "economic_distinction": "This is a state-dependent path-order statistic using a running peak, the earliest maximum-drawdown trough, and post-trough recovery. Two afternoons with the same endpoint return, amount profile, VWAP, or realized volatility can receive different values when shock timing and recovery differ. It is not a sign inversion, a window change, a terminal closing-location-only statistic, or an aggregation of return-tested factors.",
